## 15. Glossary

| Term | Meaning |
| --- | --- |
| **WIT** | Work Item Type — what kind of work this is |
| **CoS** | Class of Service — how we treat this work, based on cost of delay |
| **WIP** | Work In Progress — items started but not finished |
| **DoW** | Definition of Workflow — the explicit statement of states and policies |
| **SLE** | Service Level Expectation — probabilistic delivery promise from historical data |
| **Commitment point** | The state transition at which we promise to deliver an item |
| **Cycle time** | Elapsed time from commitment point to delivery point |
| **Lead time** | Elapsed time from customer request to delivery |
| **Throughput** | Items delivered per unit time |
| **Flow efficiency** | Active time ÷ total elapsed time |
| **Aging WIP** | How long each in-flight item has been in progress |
| **CFD** | Cumulative Flow Diagram — stacked area chart of items per state over time |
| **Little's Law** | WIP = Throughput × Cycle Time |
| **Capacity allocation** | Deliberate split of capacity across WITs |
| **Replenishment** | Moving work into the committed queue |
| **STATIK** | Systems Thinking Approach to Introducing Kanban |
| **DORA metrics** | Deployment frequency, lead time for changes, change failure rate, failed-deployment recovery time |
